@meeting vesselTestFit
// SW4, the Veyli vessel: Monday Day 29, 13:30, the machine shop bench. The new part goes into the cracked one's
// housing and spins true. Taavek's long Veyli word is never spelled out (EP1's rule for new Veyli words: ask first).
// Your two helpers react after (event.veyliVessel.testfit.<id>). Then the close.
title: The test fit
from: Taavek
gist: The new impeller went into its housing on the bench and spun true. Taavek said a long word in Veyli, then: "Good. Very good. The round one."
== lines
taavek: Now. In it goes. Slowly. You turn it.   [gesture]
taavek: Ah. Ah!   [listen]
taavek: No common word for this. In Veyli, it is long. It means: good, and also, I will tell everyone.   [laugh]
taavek > you: Good. Very good. The round one.   [nod]
? choice
* We made it together.   flavour:share rel:taavek+1
  taavek: Together. Yes. Your hands, my drawing. Good trade.   [nod]
* Tell everyone, then.   flavour:cheer rel:taavek+1
  taavek: I will! First my ship. Then everyone. Then everyone again.   [laugh]
taavek: Now I pack it. Carefully. Like an egg. A very hard egg.   [laugh]
